---
description: Next.js web app conventions — routing, i18n, components.
globs:
  - web/**
---

Canonical: `AGENTS.md`. Deep docs: `web/README.md`, `web/sanity/README.md`, `web/src/i18n/README.md`.

- i18n: field-level — thread `{ locale, siteLocale }` down every render path and resolve fields there; GROQ projects the full `{ _key, _type, language, value }` arrays.
- Server components by default; `"use client"` only for state, effects or browser APIs.
- Heavy client code that only some pages render goes behind a lazy boundary (`next/dynamic` in a `"use client"` file); CI fails a route over its first-load JS ceiling in `.github/bundle-budget.json`.
- Never read the locale from `useRouter()`, `usePathname()`, `window.location` or cookies in a module — it comes in as a prop.
- Build locale-prefixed URLs with the helpers in `web/src/i18n/`, never by concatenating prefixes.
